            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 106421,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Looks straightforward. The checklist in A3 is simple enough to do in a few minutes. The tracking sheet A6 is also clear.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 390795,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "This is a good start. For the checklist A3, should we add a point to check the remote control batteries weekly? They always die at the worst times. Also, for the tracking sheet A6, who is responsible for filling it out, and when? After every sale?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "👍",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 173570,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "What if we are too busy with customers to fill out the sheet?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Excellent point about the batteries, @390795. I'll add that as a weekly check item. For responsibility, I propose the opening staff member does the checklist A3 each morning. For the tracking sheet A6, the seller who closes the sale should fill it in immediately. It should only take 30 seconds.",
            "mentions": [
              390795
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "@173570 That's a valid concern. The idea is to make it quick enough to do right after you process the payment, before moving to the next customer. If it's really busy, you can jot it on a notepad and enter it within the hour. The key is not to leave it to the end of the day.",
            "mentions": [
              173570
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 106421,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Opening staff doing the checklist works for me. And filling the tracker right after the sale is a good habit. I can do that.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 390795,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "That process sounds robust. It assigns clear ownership and ensures the data is timely. I'm happy with that.",
